      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Let me also look at the AbstractMonitorTest base class to understand helper methods.Now I have a clear picture. Let me write the improved test with:\n1. Descriptive labels instead of cryptic single-letter ones (A/B/C/D/E/F)\n2. Clearer assertion messages\n3. Unused imports/constant removed\n4. Phase-marking commentsNow let me compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces cryptic single-letter labels (A–F) with descriptive names like `\"afterCreatingFiles\"` and `\"afterDeletingFirstFile\"`, improves assertion messages to explain intent, adds phase-marking comments, and removes unused imports and the unused `PATH_STRING_FIXTURE` constant — all without changing any method calls or expected outcomes."
